hello and welcome to the new old review  source for everything anime and manga  and today we are here to engulf  ourselves in the sheer desolation  that is the spade kingdom arc of black  clover or at least i think that's what  it might be called i don't know on the  wiki it just says arc 11 which is such a  lame name for such a powerhouse  experience and sadly no i did not reach  the end of it in one sitting i got to  around chapter 260 which felt like a  pretty depressing yet natural place to  stop with far too much to discuss as it  is and for some reference that's about  the point where the army got abducted  and asked to go left  in despair poor poor astor but at least  he has a cool sword now that  is a definite plus in any case there was  too much to discuss which was quite  problematic really just like you not  being subscribed to the new world review  problematic because how else will i know  that you would like regular  black cover content uploaded straight  into your youtube feed  hmm you gotta think about these things  but alright the premise of this arc  seems almost wildly simple  aster and select friends of asta have  been training in the heart kingdom for  the past six months during that time  asda has gotten big  very big not taller i think just wider  but still  very wide then all of a sudden the spade  kingdom invades and we spend  i think a good 30 chapters locked in  non-stop devil fraught death-defying  combat  so it's somewhat like the beginning of  the reincarnation arc in a way  just with significantly less build and  lead in time with the whole royal knight  fiasco thing  and that was definitely noticeable  tarbital wasted no time at all throwing  us straight into the deep end here and  bam before i knew it we were locked in  battle with all three of the dark  triad yeah the evil spade dudes and the  one dudette and you can more or less  divide this 30 chapter part of the arc  into a simple discussion about each one  of them the first member we were  properly introduced to being zeno who  was entrusted with the mission of  assaulting the golden dawn headquarters  in an effort to obtain william vengeance  and his delightful world tree magic and  the first thing of note is that i like  william's new lifestyle choice not to  wear his mask around all the time or  even at all that's a pretty big step  considering that he is still  cursed and everything but it is also  very thematically appropriate given that  he has nothing left to hide after that  whole  elf event so as a result there is no  internal need for a mask  and as such no need for an external mask  fantastic  as for zeno himself i have no strong  impression of him at this stage out of  the three dark triad members he's the  most stoic and serious he's your  classical cool and collected bad guy  he has a great design though i do like  the positioning of the cross on his face  i also do like his bone magic that looks  very cool but  otherwise he's just a little bit too  plain to me at this point although part  of the problem with that may be that  zeno's part of the story here is  completely overshadowed by yuno who  as it turns out is not only a member of  royalty as i've been assuming but he is  actually the last prince of the spade  kingdom  certainly wasn't quite expecting him to  be that important but it's a nice  confirmation of my working thoughts  regarding him everything just  makes perfect sense with this revealed  and by everything i mostly mean just his  natural talent  of course it does throw an interesting  question into the mix as well as the  royalty of the spade kingdom will this  impede euno's quest to become there was  a king like will he eventually take up  that sort of role but on behalf of the  spade kingdom leaving the door wide open  for astor to become the wizard king of  the clover kingdom and thus engineering  a situation  where both of them get to do that thing  that they wanted to do or maybe because  the diamond and heart kingdoms are in  ruins anyway we'll end this arc with all  four nations coming together under one  ruler  and keep that rivalry in tow i don't  know thoughts thoughts to be had by me  right now however this arc has finally  given me what i've wanted to see for  quite some time which is you know  having his arse handed to him it was  quite something to finally see yuno hit  that all-important wall that astor seems  to charge into with every minor step he  takes because yuno has never really been  put in a spot where he's had to do that  cool thing of surpassing his limits his  limits were just always naturally  outrageous but now  now he's going to have to do that exact  thing and what results is bound to be  pretty amazing although another  highlight here was the very surprising  klaus  it's now incredibly clear that he has  adopted astor's mentality and over the  past six months perhaps even more klaus  has seen himself rigorously train and  surpass his own limits as a magic knight  sadly though it did not help a whole lot  if at all in the end but i still  appreciated that character growth i also  thought that maybe  just maybe tarbata might have finally  killed someone worthwhile that's someone  being class  seeing klaus's body hanging on the verge  of death sent a sudden jolt down my  spine before i realized that this is  black clover and everyone was healed i  mean to be fair no not everyone was  healed there were heavy casualties  within the golden dawn they just  well they happened to be the characters  that we didn't know and or care about  all the ones that we did know and care  about survived so  that's convenient still we are getting  one closer to a meaningful death so i  will take it elsewhere the heart kingdom  is being invaded by our second dark  triad member veronica who i would say is  probably my favorite because she has by  far the most personality even if it is  really channeled into this  devilishly dominatrix lifestyle and who  knows perhaps that's what i like most  about her in any case she is also a lot  more meaningful at the moment because  her devil happens to be magikala the one  who cursed noelle's mother so already i  feel i have a much more vested interest  in seeing her defeat as opposed to the  other two so of course it's highly  appropriate that she became noelle's  opponent  sort of which speaking of that fight was  kind of amazing firstly i love that noel  got to show up for training on a couple  of different levels one of which would  be a new iteration of the valkyrie armor  designed specifically to allow noel to  fight within water  valkyriama mermaid edition and also noel  has this distinctly more  aster vibe going on about her now and  there was this particular moment where  she did a very astor thing which was his  trademark  suicide launch right at wanaka managing  to get in a pretty damn good strike as  well and apart from yami i really do  think that noel is one of my favorite  characters to see in combat in black  clover she has a ton of raw power a  variety of applications and now an  enduring never give up attitude clad her  in some magic warrior armor and we are  good to go  more of this plis and the heart kingdom  had a bunch of other fun fights as well  involving charmy luck and leopold i'm  not going to go into all of them in any  depth any depth at all i don't really  care enough but it was  intriguing to see the evolution of the  black clover magic system at play such  as invoking features like true magic and  arrays i always enjoy new features like  that and how they get casually  integrated into future fights like we  now have with mana zone and mana skin  and such  what i'm not quite enjoying is our new  scaling system this whole  stages thing within a couple of chapters  of being introduced it feels almost  completely meaningless because even the  fodder style disciple dudes in this arc  are automatically stage zeros and a  whole ton of our characters just sit in  the arcane stage anyway and it's just  like well why  even bother introducing the system if  everyone of importance and in fact even  those of very minimal importance like  the disciples are just always going to  be  at the top of that pyramid anyway  probably the only decent thing that  stages have going for them right now was  a brief  flashback with magna flagging him as a  stage five or whatever and is seemingly  motivating him to grow in return at some  point otherwise  i just got kind of sick of the stage  talk although nowhere near as much as  the percentage talk holy crap at some  points in this arc it felt like  old-school dragon ball z  all over again with villains claiming  that they're only using x percent of  their power and it's all just  unnecessary scaling and i feel like  they'd all be much more threatening  villains if we had no idea how close  they were to using their maximum devil  potential  which i suppose brings us to dante who  has probably the most exciting segment  getting to face off against asta and  yami before getting into that though i  do want to say that  asta has changed during these six months  and not just in terms of width either i  mean he has but also mentally he's  matured a hell of a lot which is very  apparent in his first scuffle with the  spade kingdom nobodies  during the section tabitha both drew and  wrote aston in a much more mature vein  and the way i would describe it is if  pre-time skip aster was a boy full of  baseless confidence then post-time  skipasta is a man whose confidence has a  very firmly rooted base he isn't all  talk anymore and i really like this new  version of him also he can fly on a  sword which is  that's cool and highly useful back to  dante though this is the most  interesting section because he unveils  our big plan  thing which involves a surprising  combination of yami and william  combination of arcane world tree and  dark magic required to open a magical  tree channel  known as klaiphoth or clifford i've  never really been sure which one it is  but it's a name that i'm quite familiar  with due to berserk where it gets used  for much the same sort of purpose a  bridge between worlds which is fun i do  like the idea of mixing and matching  magic like this  i mean we need an evil tree sure let's  grab the tree guy and the dark guy and  we'll smush them together  thus resulting in some sort of dark tree  i like it and the army does go on to  have a pretty spectacular battle against  dante once again doing the thing he does  and surpassing his limits right there on  the spot although on this one occasion  not even that was enough and he  implored astor for help the two of which  made a pretty fantastic team  especially right at the end were asked  to ran out of swords so yami tossed his  own to deliver the final blow it was so  damn cool and i did notice that after  the army got captured his sword was  still there so i do hope that astor  inherits it and becomes significantly  more of a badass than he already is  maybe even incorporate it into his  anti-magic shenanigans book  of course to win the fight against dante  astor also needed to have a conversation  with mr devil or i'm assuming  mr devil i don't know his or her name  yet although we get lots of other devil  names such as luciferio and zagreb the  latter of which was the name of the  devil that we had previously defeated  what we do know is that asda's devil is  seemingly very lowly ranked compared to  zagred magikala luciferio and  i don't remember the other one's name if  we did find that out  still as it turns out aston's devil is  basically the devil equivalent of astor  low ranking peasant scum so they should  make quite a great team really meanwhile  dante is defeated but not before  presenting his opposing philosophy of  only being most human when unleashing  your darkest emotions so he is being set  up disastrous polar opposite and i have  to say i was surprised that he was  actually beaten at the end especially at  a mighty 80 percent of devil power  but then again if this arc is going to  be anything like tabata's previous  entries then i imagine that ass bay trio  aren't actually going to end up as the  major climactic antagonist and there  will be someone or something or some  things plural  even bigots take down as far as the arc  goes so far though tarbeta has moved in  pretty fast and furiously i really  wasn't prepared for the speed in which  we just casually mentioned stuff like oh  yeah the diamond kingdom's been like  totally conquered off-screen well almost  totally conquered and just yeah in  general the stakes went from zero to a  thousand just in an instant and  something else i also want to ask  margaritas about i'm just curious but a  black clover chapter's shorter at this  point  it might just be because they were  mostly action based but it feels like  going through chapters took much less  time than usual i noticed that most of  them were around 15 pages which is  definitely less than your standard 18  that gets published in weekly shown and  jump for other series and i'm not sure  if it's been like that the whole time  and i just didn't notice or if at this  point  tombato is cut down for some sort of  reason in any case this whole spade  kingdom business does hold a lot of  promise i very much enjoy that we're now  getting sea devil usage beyond aster and  any time that someone accesses that  devil power it results in simply  stunning artwork from tarpita he has a  really solid mastery of how to use  shades and just pure black to great  effect as well  as a fun general devil aesthetic to play  with but really this is going to be  another long one isn't it  30 chapters or so down and i feel like  we've only just finished the  introduction this whole section was one  big showcase of initial battles and a  widespread call to action and i don't  know exactly how much of the series is  left i think it's only about 20 chapters  or so at the time of this recording  before i need to make that switch to  weekly but regardless i very much do  look forward to finishing the black  clover journey  next week and what do you guys think  please do leave your thoughts in the  comments below or even join my discord  server and if you're keen for some more  black clover content then please do feel  free to check out some of my other  videos or even subscribe to the channel  for very maybe regular black clover  goodness delivered straight into your  youtube feed but for now this has been  the new world review and i'll see you  next time

